{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790976794,"nonce":"G2YNcZZHoGItq8+Tq+YR+cmTM3s=","message":"Landed as 60017e36, on the list, the gantt and across a board's swimlanes. `doc/design/terminal-renderer.md` Rank says the rule, Board and Nesting point at it, and AGENTS.md's key paragraph has the sentence.\n\nHow it works:\n\n- `tui/nest.go` `crossGroup` finds the neighbouring group when `moveBlock` reports no sibling that way: the nearest root above (going up) or below (going down). The row keeps its place in `order` — the boundary between two groups is one point, and which group a row is in is which header it is drawn under — so the drag relabels the row's `treeRow.group` and nothing moves. The board, which has real lanes, splices the card out of its stack and into the neighbouring lane's stack in the same column, at its end going up and its start going down.\n- `tui/group.go` is the shared half: `crossing` (the group a row has been carried into and the value its field takes), `crossRefusal` and `groupValue`. What the drop writes is the value a row already in that group holds — an enum's value id, a relation's or an identity's id, a bool — and `(none)` writes null. A board lane the grabbed card emptied on its way out falls back to the card's own stored value, so carrying it down and back up again lands where it started and writes nothing.\n- The drop is one `host.IssueSet` with the rank and the field, which is one commit; on the gantt a crossing counts as a reorder even though the cursor did not move, because a row in another group has new neighbours. The status says `moved to \u003cgroup\u003e` and the cursor follows the row.\n\nRefusals, the bell and a status line, the row staying at its group's edge:\n\n- `group_by` of `type`: `type cannot be changed`. The type decides which fields an issue has, so a move does not get to change it.\n- a set-valued `group_by` (`multi-enum`, `multi-identity`, `multi-relation`): `\u003ckey\u003e: use git work issue add/remove`. A row is grouped by its whole set — `treeOrder` groups on the drawn cell, which is every value joined — so a drag cannot say which item it meant. Same rule as `Space` on such a cell.\n- a `group_by` that is not a field of the row's type: named, rather than left to the schema check after the write.\n- a nested child never crosses: `crossGroup` refuses anything below level 0.\n\nHints gained nothing: `↑↓: move` on a list and `↑↓: reorder` on a board and a gantt already cover it.\n\nTests are `tui/group_test.go`: cross down and up on a list, into `(none)`, the `type` and set-valued refusals, a nested child staying put, the gantt crossing and the board's swimlanes — each checking the field written, the operation count (two operations, which is one `set` of two keys, against the four two calls would leave), the status line and the cursor.","files":null}]}